            "The Claritin dataset consists of different male ratios and number of tweets. We compare the performance of gpt-turbo-3.5 and gpt-4 in detail by decomposing the results into each (male ratio, number of tweets) pair. Figure~\\ref{fig:model_compare} compares the gpt-turbo-3.5 and gpt-4 models in terms of the number of fairness samples on the Claritin dataset. The value $t$ in a cell means that the gpt-turbo-3.5 has $t$ more fair samples than gpt-4. As shown in the table, gpt-turbo-3.5 outperforms gpt-4 when the male ratio is 0.5 and the number of tweets is 10 while gpt-4 is better in the other cases. This shows that gpt-4 is better at processing longer tweets and the samples where the male ratio is not equal.\n",
